00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:50.610
Einstein's principle that there is no
absolute there's no point of absolute

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:56.489
rest in the universe there's no such
thing as absolute rest that's an example

00:03:56.489 --> 00:04:03.630
of a fundamental principle and from that
principle Einstein erected his theory of

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:10.770
relativity so
from with a small number of fundamental

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:16.680
principles like that one and a small
number of fundamental parameters like

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:21.750
the mass of the electron and the speed
of light science has been very

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:27.180
successful and explaining a large range
of phenomena from the orbits of planets

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:33.330
to the color of the sky to the size of
raindrops many many other phenomena

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:42.780
we've been successful in explaining and
until recently we believed that given a

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:50.030
small number of fundamental laws and
parameters that there was only one

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:55.920
universe that was possible
one unique universe like a crossword

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:04.200
puzzle that has only one solution very
recently we've learned that this belief

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:10.830
is probably wrong starting with the same
fundamental principles the same

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:17.700
fundamental laws and the same parameters
it appears that a large variety of

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:24.300
universes is possible with many
different properties some universes

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:29.870
might have 17 dimensions or 23
dimensions some of them might have

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:35.940
complex molecules like DNA and
hemoglobin is in our universe some of

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:41.580
them may have only subatomic particles
some of them may have planets and stars

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:48.470
like in our universe some may be
completely empty

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:57.360
some may have conditions that allow life
to emerge and some may not it appears

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.470
that our particular universe is just an
accident

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:09.000
a random throw of the dice and if so
there are many properties of our

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:14.220
universe that are incalculable from
fundamental laws that we have to just

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:21.870
take as accidents this collection of all
possible universes is called the multi

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:27.660
and some of you may have heard that term
before it sounds like a word and one of

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:32.510
Robert Heinlein science fiction novels

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:41.850
needless to say these recent findings
are very upsetting to scientists and

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:47.820
especially to theoretical physicists
theoretical physicists want to be able

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:54.150
to explain all the properties of our
universe as necessary consequences of a

00:06:54.150 --> 00:07:00.000
small number of fundamental laws and
parameters and to find out that they

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.790
cannot do that that there are a huge
number of universes possible from the

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:10.229
same starting point with many different
properties that's a very upsetting and

00:07:10.229 --> 00:07:16.880
let me try to give you an analogy it's
sort of like going into a shoe store and

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:24.449
finding that an eye a size 9 shoe fits
you in a size 12 fits you equally well

00:07:24.449 --> 00:07:39.720
and a size 15 fits you equally well so
why has our belief changed recently for

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:46.289
two reasons
one to explain certain I'd odd features

00:07:46.289 --> 00:07:51.660
of our universe and secondly because
there are actually some modern theories

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:57.560
of physics that predict the multiverse
to predict this large number of

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:06.770
universes so I want to say a little bit
about these two things now back in the

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:09.770
1960s

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:16.490
physicists noticed that certain
parameters of our universe appear to be

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:23.610
fine-tuned for the emergence of life and
when I say life I don't mean life like

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:29.460
human beings or even life like on our
planet I mean life of any form and when

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:35.080
I may mean when I say fine-tuned I mean
that if certain parameters were a little

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:40.440
little larger than they actually are or
a little smaller than they actually are

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:47.620
that life could never have arisen in our
universe one example is the strength of

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:53.140
the nuclear force the nuclear force is
the force that holds the subatomic

00:08:53.140 --> 00:09:00.730
particles the neutrons and the protons
together at the centres of atoms and if

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:06.430
the nuclear force were only a few
percent larger than what it actually is

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:13.540
in our universe then all of the hydrogen
in the early universe would have fused

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:18.670
with helium
she would have fused to make helium it

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:23.290
would have fused together to make helium
there would be no hydrogen left in our

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:30.970
universe and no hydrogen means no water
and biologists agree that probably you

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:37.180
need water to have life on the other
hand if the nuclear force were just a

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:43.270
little bit weaker than it is then you
would not be able to create complex

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:51.460
atoms like carbon silicon nitrogen that
we think are almost certainly necessary

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:58.060
for life so the the actual value of the
nuclear force in our universe lies

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:05.490
within a narrow range to allow the
emergence of life another example of

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:12.610
this fine-tuning is what astronomers and
physicists call dark energy and this was

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:19.990
discovered recently in the in the late
1990s dark energy is an energy that

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:25.780
pervades all of space we call it dark
because we can't see it and it leads to

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:32.130
a effective anti gravitational force
normal gravity pulls things together

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:39.610
dark energy leads to a gravitational
force that pushes things apart so when

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:43.930
we look at distant galaxies we actually
see them accelerating away from each

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:51.519
other by measure
the rate of expansion of the universe we

00:10:51.519 --> 00:10:56.410
know the universe is expanding and with
the discovery of dark energy we actually

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:00.609
see that it's accelerating not just
expanding but it's like somebody has

00:11:00.609 --> 00:11:06.579
their foot down on the cosmic gas pedal
and by measuring the rate of expansion

00:11:06.579 --> 00:11:14.949
of the universe in different epochs of
time we can calculate the the value of

00:11:14.949 --> 00:11:20.169
the dark energy how much dark energy
there is and it's a particular number

00:11:20.169 --> 00:11:26.970
it's about 100,000 I'm sorry 100
millionth of an ERG per cubic centimeter

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:32.889
now an herb that's a unit of energy if I
drop a penny a penny on the floor from

00:11:32.889 --> 00:11:39.459
waist-high that's a few hundred thousand
herbs so 100 millionth of an herb per

00:11:39.459 --> 00:11:47.919
cubic centimeter may not sound seem like
very much energy but space is very large

00:11:47.919 --> 00:11:53.169
just in this room here there are
thousands of herbs of dark energy just

00:11:53.169 --> 00:11:58.419
in this auditorium and if you go to the
reaches of space two stars and galaxies

00:11:58.419 --> 00:12:03.609
that builds up to a very very large
amount of dark energy because the

00:12:03.609 --> 00:12:08.649
volumes are so large but the important
point here is that we've measured a

00:12:08.649 --> 00:12:14.139
specific value of this dark energy one
hundred millionth of an herb per cubic

00:12:14.139 --> 00:12:24.429
centimeter now here's where the rub
comes in the fine tuning if the dark

00:12:24.429 --> 00:12:32.109
energy were just a little bit larger
than it actually is then the universe

00:12:32.109 --> 00:12:37.779
would expand so rapidly would accelerate
so rapidly that matter would never be

00:12:37.779 --> 00:12:47.079
able to clump together to form stars and
planets because it would be dispersing

00:12:47.079 --> 00:12:53.229
too rapidly to cluster together to make
planets and stars and if the dark energy

00:12:53.229 --> 00:12:59.679
were just a little bit less than it
actually is then the universe would have

00:12:59.679 --> 00:13:06.160
rika elapsed long before you could form
stars and we all all scientists agree

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:12.340
that the chemical elements and the
planet in our bodies heavier than

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:17.110
hydrogen were made at the Centers of
stars so you have to form a star in

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:22.990
order to form chemical elements and
unique chemical elements to make life to

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:28.840
give you an idea of how narrow this
range is the dark energy must be to

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:37.480
allow the emergence of life starting
from the same fundamental laws the dark

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:44.230
energy could be anywhere from trillions
of trillions of trillions of herbs per

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:50.560
cubic centimeter to one to one
trillionth of went to two- trillions of

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:55.900
trillions of trillions of herbs per
cubic centimeter and the value in our

00:13:55.900 --> 00:14:01.600
universe happens to be only one hundred
thousand one hundred millionth of an

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:07.510
herb per centimeter that is very close
to the middle of that enormous range if

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.670
we're just a little bit bigger or a
little bit smaller than it actually is

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:18.490
then life could never have emerged in
our universe so these are two examples

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:23.530
of parameters the strength of the
nuclear force and the value of the dark

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:28.830
energy and our universe that appear to
lie within a very narrow range

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:33.520
permitting the emergence of life either
a little bigger or a little smaller than

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:43.510
they actually are life could not have
arisen so the great question is why why

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:50.560
do the parameters of our universe appear
to be finely tuned as our universe care

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:56.170
about life after all we can we could
have a universe of totally inanimate

00:14:56.170 --> 00:15:02.020
matter well there are a couple of
different explanations or answers to

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:10.060
this question why one is intelligent
design perhaps there was an intelligent

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:16.300
being that created the universe and that
being wanted there to be life and

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:21.490
for that being tuned the parameters
created the parameters of the universe

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:26.860
to allow the emergence of life that's
one explanation but for the the great

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:38.200
majority of scientists the intelligent
design argument is not appealing so

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:42.880
there's another explanation which does
not require an intelligent designer and

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:50.500
that is the multiverse according to the
multiverse there are lots of different

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:56.590
universes with many different of the
fundamental parameters some with nuclear

00:15:56.590 --> 00:16:01.300
forces much larger than the nuclear
force in our universe some with nuclear

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:06.280
forces much smaller than the nuclear
force in our universe some with what

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:10.990
much larger values of dark energy than
in our universe some with much smaller

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:21.120
values of dark energy and in most of
these universes will be dead lifeless

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:30.490
conglomerations of matter and energy but
we by definition because we're here to

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:35.440
talk about it we live in one of the
small fraction of universes that have

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:40.840
the right values of those parameters to
allow the emergence of life to allow the

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:46.480
creation of stars to allow the creation
of planets to allow the creation of

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:54.310
complex molecules we have to inhabit
such a universe or we wouldn't be here

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:59.830
but you can see that the multiverse
explanation does not require a divine

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:09.100
creator an intelligent designer an
analogy to this kind of explanation of

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:16.690
the fine-tuning is the following suppose
we began wondering why it is that the

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:24.430
earth has such amenable conditions for
life we have a magnetic field that

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:30.160
shields us from that from the solar wind
which would be very devastating to lie

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:36.040
we have oxygen we have water we're at
the right temperature from our Sun so

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:41.770
that is not too hot and not too cold
waters not evaporated it's not frozen

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:48.490
it's in liquid form which is very
conducive to life and so why is it that

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:55.590
Earth has has all of these wonderful
conditions aren't we lucky so we might

00:17:55.590 --> 00:18:01.000
we might begin wondering about that and
asking how that came about

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:06.220
we might propose that some does
intelligence designer created the earth

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:10.600
this way for our benefit but then we
look at other planets in our solar

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:15.190
system and we find that there are a
range of different atmospheres and

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:20.590
temperatures and so on that are not
conducive to life for example on Uranus

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:30.340
the temperature is minus 371 degrees
Fahrenheit very very cold and on Venus

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:37.860
the rain is sulfuric acid so when all of
the other parameters in our solar system

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:42.970
conditions are not right for life we are
on a planet that has the right

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:49.240
conditions for life because otherwise we
wouldn't be here to talk about it so the

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:55.780
decimal nation of the multiverse that is
an explanation for the fine-tuning of

00:18:55.780 --> 00:19:02.320
our universe as a whole is very similar
to this analogy with the conditions of

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:12.760
life on Earth however there's a
trade-off for scientists in accepting

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:20.650
the multiverse explanation of the
fine-tuning that trade-off is that the

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:25.900
historic mission of science and a
special historic mission of physics to

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:32.110
be able to explain all the properties of
our universe as necessary consequences

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:40.930
of a small number of fundamental laws
that historic mission is futile many of

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:43.210
the properties of our universe are what
they are

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:46.299
just
by accident and there are other

00:19:46.299 --> 00:19:51.630
universes with very different properties
starting from the same fundamental laws

00:19:51.630 --> 00:20:00.460
are we are here because our universe is
what it is our universe is what it is

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:10.960
because we are here and let me give
another analogy suppose that we have a

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:21.580
population of very intelligent fish and
the fish began to argue the fish notice

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:27.549
that that their world is full of water
which is very nice for the existence of

00:20:27.549 --> 00:20:36.399
fish and they began to argue about why
it's all water and some of the

00:20:36.399 --> 00:20:42.640
theoretical fish say well there's
probably a reason from fundamental

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:47.049
principles why the world has to be water
and they've been calculating and

00:20:47.049 --> 00:20:52.360
calculating and calculating to show why
everything must be water and they never

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:56.309
can quote they're never quite up to the
task

00:20:56.320 --> 00:21:02.380
and then one day a group of wizened old
fish says that maybe they're just

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:09.250
fooling themselves maybe there are other
worlds that don't have water that are

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:14.740
dry and they just happen to live in a
world with water because otherwise they

00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:23.020
wouldn't be there so let me turn now to
a couple of modern theories of physics

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:28.419
that actually predict the existence of
the multiverse the argument I've given

00:21:28.419 --> 00:21:34.899
so far is really not a prediction it's
an explanation of this fine-tuning

00:21:34.899 --> 00:21:40.000
observation that was made in the 1960s
that the parameters of our universe

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:45.130
appear to be finely tuned to allow the
existence of of life there are actually

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:50.770
some theories in physics that predict
the existence of other universes one is

00:21:50.770 --> 00:21:58.120
string theory which was formulated in
the late 1960s and onward

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:06.940
string theory is a fundamental theory of
physics that attempts to unify all of

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:12.610
the different forces that we not know
and it rests on a fundamental principle

00:22:12.610 --> 00:22:19.950
that the the basic constituents of
matter are not particles but tiny

00:22:19.950 --> 00:22:25.930
one-dimensional vibrations of energy
that are called strings and from those

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:32.980
vibrations all the forces and particles
that we know of are produced another

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:39.010
aspect of string theory is that in
addition to the three dimensions that we

00:22:39.010 --> 00:22:44.860
know about there are seven additional
spatial dimensions we don't see them

00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:50.860
because they are curled up in tiny loops
ultra tiny loops like looking at a

00:22:50.860 --> 00:22:55.150
garden hose from it from a distance and
if you look at it from a distance it

00:22:55.150 --> 00:22:58.570
looks just like a one-dimensional line
you can't see the other dimensions

00:22:58.570 --> 00:23:03.700
because they're too far away that's sort
of the way these ultra tiny dimensions

00:23:03.700 --> 00:23:09.790
of string theory behave now there's been
no confirmation no no experimental

00:23:09.790 --> 00:23:14.230
confirmation of string theory to date
but some of the brightest theoretical

00:23:14.230 --> 00:23:18.210
physicists in the world have been
working on it for 40 years

00:23:18.210 --> 00:23:25.870
well these extra seven dimensions of
string theory were folded up into a very

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:33.010
tiny size to make only three large-scale
dimensions that we experienced and it

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:36.160
turns out that there are zillions of
different ways that these other

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:40.450
dimensions can be folded up like many
many different ways of phoning up a

00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:45.060
piece of paper and each different way of
folding up these other seven dimensions

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:51.420
corresponds to a different universe with
different properties so string theory

00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:57.010
predicts that there are many many other
different universes besides ours with

00:23:57.010 --> 00:24:05.250
different properties there's another
theory of modern physics called internal

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:11.430
eternal inflation which also predicts
the multiverse

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:17.610
inflation is an idea which does have
some experimental confirmation and the

00:24:17.610 --> 00:24:25.350
idea is that when the universe was very
very young a tiny fraction of a second

00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:32.640
old it began expanding exponentially
fast and then after a split second

00:24:32.640 --> 00:24:42.840
resumed the leisurely rate of expansion
of the standard Big Bang model and one

00:24:42.840 --> 00:24:47.940
of the aspects of the inflation theory
as it has been developed more and more

00:24:47.940 --> 00:24:55.320
in the last decades as that space in
this early period of time when the

00:24:55.320 --> 00:24:59.400
universe was a tiny fraction of a second
